WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.417
Narrator: Spider-Man is back!

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:05.961
Ned: Awesome!

00:00:05.961 --> 00:00:08.537
Narrator:After the tragic
ending of "Infinity War"

00:00:08.537 --> 00:00:10.130
a lot of us were worried about the future

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:12.274
of our favorite web-slinger.

00:00:12.274 --> 00:00:14.441
But Tom Holland returns
in this fresh trailer

00:00:14.441 --> 00:00:16.534
for "Spider-Man: Far From Home."

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:17.890
Although, it may leave you

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:20.806
with more questions than answers.

00:00:20.806 --> 00:00:22.019
Peter: What just happened?

00:00:22.019 --> 00:00:24.019
Narrator: Does "Far From
Home" take place before

00:00:24.019 --> 00:00:25.900
or after "Avengers: Endgame?"

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.698
Who are the villains in this movie?

00:00:27.698 --> 00:00:31.781
And who's Jake Gyllenhaal
supposed to be playing?

00:00:32.694 --> 00:00:34.971
To start, "Spider-Man: Far From Home"

00:00:34.971 --> 00:00:36.928
appears to take place after the events

00:00:36.928 --> 00:00:38.859
of "Avengers: Endgame."

00:00:38.859 --> 00:00:40.572
Sony producer Amy Pascal revealed

00:00:40.572 --> 00:00:43.217
that "Spider-Man: Far
From Home" takes place

00:00:43.217 --> 00:00:45.755
just a few minutes after
the end of "Endgame."

00:00:45.755 --> 00:00:47.589
That makes this trailer extra special

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:49.815
being the only way to
get a peek at the world

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:52.075
after "Endgame" premieres this April.

00:00:52.075 --> 00:00:54.200
And, let's be honest, we're all curious

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.724
who's going to survive
the Mad Titan's invasion.

00:00:56.724 --> 00:00:58.224
So, let's take a closer look.

00:00:59.124 --> 00:01:02.340
A lot of familiar faces make
a return in this trailer.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.643
Marissa Tomei returns as Aunt May

00:01:04.643 --> 00:01:06.191
who discovered Peter Parker's secret

00:01:06.191 --> 00:01:07.919
at the end of "Homecoming."

00:01:07.919 --> 00:01:09.356
Aunt May seems to have adjusted to

00:01:09.356 --> 00:01:11.562
Peter's alter-ego as the two play a part

00:01:11.562 --> 00:01:13.251
in running a homeless shelter

00:01:13.251 --> 00:01:16.697
a story line from both the
comics and the PS4 video game.

00:01:16.697 --> 00:01:18.816
John Favreau is back as Happy Hogan

00:01:18.816 --> 00:01:21.188
who was a big part in the first film.

00:01:21.188 --> 00:01:23.526
He shows up with a check
from Synchrony Bank

00:01:23.526 --> 00:01:25.035
a little nod to the actual bank

00:01:25.035 --> 00:01:26.918
that issues Marvel credit cards.

00:01:26.918 --> 00:01:29.176
And it seems that Aunt May and Happy Hogan

00:01:29.176 --> 00:01:31.325
might just be more than friends.

00:01:31.325 --> 00:01:32.158
Happy: New dress?

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.491
Aunt May: Yes it is. How'd you know?

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:37.722
Peter: What just happened?

00:01:37.722 --> 00:01:39.388
Narrator: The trailer
also nods to a character

00:01:39.388 --> 00:01:43.315
we're all familiar with, but
have never seen in the MCU.

00:01:43.315 --> 00:01:45.389
Uncle Ben, hinted at by the initials

00:01:45.389 --> 00:01:48.213
on the suitcase that
Peter brings to Europe.

00:01:48.213 --> 00:01:50.761
Peter is not alone on his trip to Europe.

00:01:50.761 --> 00:01:54.099
Zendaya returns as Michelle "M.J." Jones

00:01:54.099 --> 00:01:56.403
the movie's version of Mary Jane Watson.

00:01:56.403 --> 00:01:58.734
It appears that M.J. will
be Peter's love interest

00:01:58.734 --> 00:02:00.825
as their romance is heavily foreshadowed

00:02:00.825 --> 00:02:01.796
throughout the trailer.

00:02:01.796 --> 00:02:03.336
Peter: I just want to
spend some time with MJ.

00:02:03.336 --> 00:02:04.921
I think she really likes me, dude.

00:02:04.921 --> 00:02:06.605
Narrator: And Flash
Thompson, who just like

00:02:06.605 --> 00:02:08.668
in the comics, bullies Peter Parker

00:02:08.668 --> 00:02:11.391
but ironically admires
Spider-Man as a hero.

00:02:11.391 --> 00:02:12.566
Flash: What? He looks
out for the neighborhood,

00:02:12.566 --> 00:02:15.109
has a dope suit, and I really respect him.

00:02:15.109 --> 00:02:16.202
Sup, dickwad?

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.268
Narrator: And of course, how can we

00:02:17.268 --> 00:02:19.250
forget Peter's best friend, Ned?

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:20.253
Ned: Awesome!

00:02:20.253 --> 00:02:22.419
Narrator: Which leads to
our first surprising reveal

00:02:22.419 --> 00:02:23.881
the return of Nick Fury.

00:02:23.881 --> 00:02:27.190
Considering Fury died after
the events of "Infinity War"

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:29.936
it seems like the character
will be brought back to life.

00:02:29.936 --> 00:02:31.643
And judging by his first words

00:02:31.643 --> 00:02:35.907
Nick: So nice to finally
meet you, Spider-Man.

00:02:35.907 --> 00:02:37.183
Narrator: It seems as though they do not

00:02:37.183 --> 00:02:38.824
encounter each other in "Endgame."

00:02:38.824 --> 00:02:41.276
And, is this figure
next to Fury Maria Hill

00:02:41.276 --> 00:02:42.752
also brought back from the dead?

00:02:42.752 --> 00:02:45.016
Or someone else entirely?

00:02:45.016 --> 00:02:46.987
A character obviously
missing from the trailer

00:02:46.987 --> 00:02:48.864
is none other than Tony Stark

00:02:48.864 --> 00:02:50.404
who is heavily featured with Spider-Man in

00:02:50.404 --> 00:02:53.572
both his first appearance in
"Civil War" and "Homecoming."

00:02:53.572 --> 00:02:54.667
And this line from Hogan

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:55.988
Happy: You're all alone.

00:02:55.988 --> 00:02:57.717
Narrator: Sounds quite ominous.

00:02:57.717 --> 00:02:59.287
Could this be hinting at the death

00:02:59.287 --> 00:03:01.439
of Tony Stark in "Avengers: Endgame?"

00:03:01.439 --> 00:03:02.596
Or maybe it's just Marvel trying

00:03:02.596 --> 00:03:04.439
to throw us off the plot.

00:03:04.439 --> 00:03:06.357
Whatever happens, the future doesn't look

00:03:06.357 --> 00:03:08.524
so promising for Iron Man.

00:03:10.241 --> 00:03:12.374
Also featured in the
trailer, are the many suits

00:03:12.374 --> 00:03:14.731
Peter wears during his trip in Europe.

00:03:14.731 --> 00:03:16.732
In the beginning, Peter wears the classic

00:03:16.732 --> 00:03:19.570
red and blue suit that
we saw in "Homecoming."

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:22.150
Of course, things don't
go according to plan

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:23.472
as Nick Fury makes an appearance

00:03:23.472 --> 00:03:25.377
to set Peter on a mission.

00:03:25.377 --> 00:03:27.947
We see two main suits
featured in the trailer.

00:03:27.947 --> 00:03:30.373
One suit that closely
resembles the classic suit

00:03:30.373 --> 00:03:33.046
but with a darker palette and wings!

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:35.686
The same wings we only
briefly saw in Homecoming

00:03:35.686 --> 00:03:37.632
are now featured more prominently

00:03:37.632 --> 00:03:39.776
seemingly allowing Peter to effortlessly

00:03:39.776 --> 00:03:41.578
glide through the sky.

00:03:41.578 --> 00:03:43.966
We also get a better look at the Noir suit

00:03:43.966 --> 00:03:47.099
from the "Spider-Man: Noir"
series set in 1933, also

00:03:47.099 --> 00:03:49.911
featured recently in "Spider-Man:
Into the Spider-Verse"

00:03:49.911 --> 00:03:51.560
voiced by Nicholas Cage.

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.252
Judging by the nighttime setting

00:03:53.252 --> 00:03:54.516
maybe this is the suit of choice

00:03:54.516 --> 00:03:58.233
when the job requires stealth
over, well, aesthetics.

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:02.400
It was long rumored
that a group of villains

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:03.880
known as the Elementals were going

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.202
to make an appearance in the film.

00:04:06.202 --> 00:04:07.865
The Elementals first made an appearance

00:04:07.865 --> 00:04:09.871
in the series, "Supernatural Thrillers"

00:04:09.871 --> 00:04:12.477
and are composed of four
extra-dimensional villains

00:04:12.477 --> 00:04:14.438
who each control different elements.

00:04:14.438 --> 00:04:16.416
Hellfire, who controls fire

00:04:16.416 --> 00:04:18.324
Hydron, who controls water

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:21.076
and Magnum, who
manipulates earth and rock.

00:04:21.076 --> 00:04:22.767
The only one missing is Zephyr

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:24.897
who has the power to control air.

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.964
But Zephyr's presence
is possibly hinted at

00:04:26.964 --> 00:04:30.249
by this lightning when they
attack the London Bridge.

00:04:30.249 --> 00:04:31.932
These villains, however, could also

00:04:31.932 --> 00:04:35.114
be Sandman, Molten Man, and Hydro-Man

00:04:35.114 --> 00:04:36.586
other super villains who also

00:04:36.586 --> 00:04:39.648
control different elements
to fight against Spider-Man.

00:04:39.648 --> 00:04:42.964
This is hinted at by these
numbers on the boat behind Ned.

00:04:42.964 --> 00:04:47.721
ASM 212, alluding to the
"Amazing Spider-Man" issue 212

00:04:47.721 --> 00:04:50.453
where Hydro-Man makes
his first appearance.

00:04:50.453 --> 00:04:52.387
Whether the villains are
really the Elementals

00:04:52.387 --> 00:04:55.649
or someone else, we'll
have to wait and see.

00:04:55.649 --> 00:04:58.230
Last, but most importantly, we finally

00:04:58.230 --> 00:04:59.906
get our first look at Mysterio

00:04:59.906 --> 00:05:01.590
one of Spider-Man's main villains

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:03.390
played by Jake Gyllenhaal.

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:05.358
Fans of the original comic will be happy

00:05:05.358 --> 00:05:08.645
to see him in the fishbowl
helmet featured in the comics.

00:05:08.645 --> 00:05:10.714
The only difference is that it seems

00:05:10.714 --> 00:05:13.077
as though Mysterio is on Spider-Man's side

00:05:13.077 --> 00:05:15.329
fighting against the bad guys.

00:05:15.329 --> 00:05:16.854
There have been numerous rumors

00:05:16.854 --> 00:05:18.678
about Nick Fury teaming Spider-Man up

00:05:18.678 --> 00:05:20.846
with Mysterio to fight the Elementals

00:05:20.846 --> 00:05:24.877
and Mysterio being a complex,
morally ambiguous villain.

00:05:24.877 --> 00:05:27.170
So, how does Mysterio go from fighting

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:30.060
alongside Spider-Man to
fighting against him?

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:32.842
Or, to speculate a bit, is it possible

00:05:32.842 --> 00:05:34.486
that The Elementals are actually

00:05:34.486 --> 00:05:37.078
just an illusion created by Mysterio

00:05:37.078 --> 00:05:38.558
whose main power in the comics

00:05:38.558 --> 00:05:41.720
is creating illusions
to deceive his enemies?

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:43.553
A similar storyline was featured

00:05:43.553 --> 00:05:45.397
in the animated series of Spider-Man

00:05:45.397 --> 00:05:47.124
where Mysterio used illusions

00:05:47.124 --> 00:05:49.567
to manipulate the city,
painting Spider-Man

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:52.297
as the villain and himself as the hero.

00:05:52.297 --> 00:05:53.488
Could this possibly be

00:05:53.488 --> 00:05:55.150
what we're seeing in the trailer?

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:56.259
It seems like Peter's friends

00:05:56.259 --> 00:05:59.071
are convinced that he's a hero.

00:05:59.071 --> 00:06:00.286
Kids: Who is that guy?

00:06:00.286 --> 00:06:02.615
- He's like Iron Man and
Thor rolled into one.

00:06:02.615 --> 00:06:04.174
Narrator: Are you convinced?

00:06:04.174 --> 00:06:06.726
So, what did you think about this trailer?

00:06:06.726 --> 00:06:08.781
What are your theories and speculations?

00:06:08.781 --> 00:06:09.614
Leave it in the comments,

00:06:09.614 --> 00:06:12.614
and see you at the theaters in July.

